-- title:
--   Integrality of the full-level moduli ring over A[j₀]
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian commutative ring and let $q$, $\ell$, $M'$ be natural numbers with $q$ and $\ell$ prime, $M' \neq 0$, $\ell \geq 3$, and with $\ell$, $M'$, $2$ and $3$ invertible in $A$. Assume two equivariance hypotheses: for every $A$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and every variable change $C$, a level-$\ell$ datum $D = (x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ satisfying `IsLevelPStructure` for $\ell$ (both pairs satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation, $\operatorname{pre}\Psi_\ell$ vanishes at $x_P$ and at $x_Q$, and the two elements $\mathrm{indepElt}$ formed from $(x_P,x_Q)$ and from $(x_Q,x_P)$ are units) transports to the corresponding datum `D.variableChange C` for $C \bullet W$; and likewise the predicate `IsGamma0PowAt` for $W$, $p$, $k$ and a polynomial $h$ (the `IsTwoKernel` condition when $p^k = 2$, and otherwise the `IsCyclicGenKernel` condition: $\deg h \le \varphi(p^k)/2$, leading coefficient $1$ in that degree, $h \cdot \operatorname{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}} \mid \operatorname{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$, and $h$ divides the relevant multiplication numerators) transports to `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h` for $C \bullet W$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the graded projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A$-algebras, assumed chord–tangent (over every field it is computed by a bijection with the affine point group compatible with addition and with Galois twisting) and origin-identity (its unit section arises from a ring map on the origin chart killing $x/y$ and $z/y$); let $\mathcal{T}$ be a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ and $q$, that is, functorial maps and variable-change actions on raw pairs of sections preserving the predicate of being a Drinfeld $q$-basis, and assume $\mathcal{T}$ is a section transport, so that these operations agree with the induced maps of $\mathrm{Proj}$'s on the underlying sections. Assume further that every variable change and every coefficient homomorphism of projective models is realised by a graded ring homomorphism $\varphi$ satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`, and such that the irrelevant ideal of the target is contained in the image ideal of the irrelevant ideal of the source. Finally let $P_0$ be an abstract level moduli package for the level moduli datum attached to `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q …`, whose points over $T$ are variable-change classes of Weierstrass curves over $T$ with unit discriminant equipped with a tuple consisting of $\Gamma_0$-kernel polynomials for the prime powers dividing $M'$, a level-$\ell$ datum and a Drinfeld $q$-basis pair, with $j$-invariant as structure map: thus $P_0$ consists of an $A$-algebra $B_0$, a universal point over $B_0$, and the property that for every $A$-algebra $T$ and every point $x$ over $T$ there is a unique $A$-algebra map $B_0 \to T$ carrying the universal point to $x$. Assume $B_0$ is of finite type over $A$. Then $B_0$ is integral over the $A$-subalgebra of $B_0$ generated by the universal $j$-invariant `P₀.j₀`.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic form of the finiteness of the fine moduli scheme of elliptic curves with full level structure over the $j$-line (Katz–Mazur 4.7.1, 5.1.1), here for the combined $\Gamma_0(M')$, level-$\ell$ and Drinfeld level-$q$ moduli problem over a Noetherian base in which $2$, $3$, $\ell$ and $M'$ are invertible. It is the integrality clause of the full-level representability statement, and is used in the analysis of minimal primes over $A[j_0]$ and in the classification of points with finite residue field.
